      "gap": "The source's normal benchmark on p. 17 is used to compare the Hoeffding bounds with the normal-case exponential bound exp(-nt^2/(2 sigma^2)) of (2.16): (2.2) with mu>=1/2 equals the right side of (2.16) in the binomial case (2.5); Theorem 2's bound (2.6) equals it when Pr{X_i=a_i}=Pr{X_i=b_i}=1/2; Bernstein's bound and Theorem 3's bounds are close to it for small lambda. Body lines 192-233 give only Phi(-y)<=exp(-y^2/2), the Mills-ratio bounds and the CLT tail; neither (2.16) in its sigma/t form nor any of these comparisons is written. Also absent is footnote 4's assertion that in Theorem 3 the upper bound X_i<=b is crucial to any improvement over the Chebyshev/Cantelli bound (1.6); only the Markov-attainment half of the footnote is at body lines 220-222 / annex lines 363-369.",
